# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics Package
- Added `@vercel/analytics` dependency to package.json
- Updated package-lock.json with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Modified app/layout.tsx
- Imported the Analytics component from '@vercel/analytics/next'
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the body section of the root layout
- Placed the Analytics component after the main content to follow best practices

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I implemented the framework-specific instructions for Next.js App Router:

1. Used npm (the project's package manager) to install @vercel/analytics
2. Imported the Analytics component using the Next.js-specific import path
3. Added the component inside the <body> tag of the root layout file
4. Maintained the existing code structure and styling

## Verification

✅ Package installation successful (369 packages added)
✅ TypeScript compilation passed with no errors
✅ Build completed successfully
✅ No type errors or linting issues introduced

## Next Steps

To enable analytics in production:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Vercel dashboard
3. Select "Analytics" from the sidebar
4. Choose this project and click "Enable"
5. Analytics will begin collecting data after the next deployment

The Analytics component will automatically track page views and web vitals once enabled in the Vercel dashboard.
